1.what are Recording rules (deep dive)

Recording rules are Prometheus rules that precompute frequently used or expensive PromQL queries and store their results as new time-series metrics.

2.What are Alerting Rules in Prometheus?

Alerting rules are Prometheus rules that continuously evaluate PromQL expressions and trigger alerts when defined conditions are met for a specified duration.

When an alert fires, Prometheus sends it to Alertmanager, which handles notification, grouping, deduplication, and routing.
